## About

This PR increases the target area for clicking on the slider line (to update a slider value) or to click and drag on the slider bar (to move a slider range).

Currently, these touch areas are driven by the width of the line and bar, which are both quite small by default and can be styled to be even thinner. (The default slider line/bar width is 8px.) This PR increases these target areas using `::before` pseudo-elements to be the height of the slider handle (the line target area is highlighted in peach, the bar target area in light purple).

![image](https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/assets/5420529/a483e94c-e51f-4a1b-8c72-d6347046f6c9)

## Notes

This change required a small adjustment to the `z-index`es used throughout the slider. I chose the smallest possible numbers for each updated `z-index`. In short, we needed to ensure the following order

1. Line target area
2. Bar target area is above the line target area
3. The handle is above the bar
4. The animation buttons are above the line target area

I used the patch file to update the theme. Note that `tools/updateIonRangeSlider.R` wants to re-add `ionrangeslider` to the `package.json`, but I didn't commit these changes.

