Closes #3139. This PR changes `reactive`, `observe`, and `render` functions so that they do not unwrap quosures on creation.

For example, this app now works:

```R
library(shiny)
library(dplyr)

shinyApp(
  fluidPage(
    checkboxGroupInput("vars", "Vars", names(mtcars)),
    tableOutput("tbl")
  ),
  function(input, output) {
    output$tbl <- renderTable({
      req(input$vars)
      mtcars %>% select(!!!input$vars)
    })
  }
)
```

It is possible to use quosures by using the `inject()` function from the upcoming version of rlang (https://github.com/r-lib/rlang/pull/591) to inject a quosure into the call:

```R
library(shiny)
library(dplyr)
librarty(rlang)

shinyApp(
  fluidPage(
    checkboxGroupInput("vars", "Vars", names(mtcars)),
    tableOutput("tbl")
  ),
  function(input, output) {
    q <- quo({
      req(input$vars)
      mtcars[, input$vars, drop = FALSE]
    })
    
    output$tbl <- inject(renderTable(!!q))
  }
)
```

