Currently, if attempting to use `nearPoints` or `brushedPoints` with ggplot where either x or y is a transformation and not just a raw data column, the functions will either fail silently without error or in the case of brushedPoints and `allRows = TRUE` give a cryptic error message about replacement having zero rows. While the documentation of brushedPoints mentions the need to use raw column names, the lack of an informative error message can make it hard to identify this issue when working on an app.

This PR proposes to detect such cases where the `xvar` or `yvar` is not in the data and give an informative error message. Perhaps additional text in error message about potential cause being ggplot2 and transformed variables would be even more informative.

Here is a minimal example app that upon brushing shows the cryptic error message with current shiny (and new more informative message with PR version):

