This PR adds the ability for Shiny apps to reconnect -- the existing input values are sent to a new session on the server side. It's designed to work with rstudio/shiny-server#440.

This reconnection behavior is opt-in. To enable, the app should call `session$allowReconnect(TRUE)`. Here's an example app:

``` R
shinyApp(
  ui = fluidPage(sidebarLayout(
    sidebarPanel(
      sliderInput("bins", "Number of bins:", min = 1, max = 50, value = 30)
    ),
    mainPanel(
      plotOutput("distPlot")
    )
  )),
  server = function(input, output, session) {
    output$distPlot <- renderPlot({
      hist(rnorm(100), breaks = input$bins)
    })

    # Set this to "force" instead of TRUE for testing locally (without Shiny Server)
    session$allowReconnect(TRUE)
  }
)
```

This closes #936, by using the `setAttribute()` function to set attributes instead of setting properties on the object.

With this test app and the existing Shiny code, `class` doesn't get set on the DOM element, because their corresponding property names in the Javascript object is `className`. Similarly, `style` of the DOEM element doesn't get set properly, because the JS object's `style` property is another object, not a CSS string.

With this patch, both the `class` and `style` of the DOM object get set properly.

``` R
shinyApp(
  ui = fluidPage(
    sliderInput("opacity", "Opacity", 0, 1, 1, step = 0.1),
    plotOutput("plot1")
  ),

  server = function(input, output) {
    output$plot1 <- renderImage({
      outfile <- tempfile(fileext='.png')

      png(outfile, width=400, height=400)
      hist(rnorm(200))
      dev.off()

      list(
        src = outfile,
        alt = "This is alternate text",
        class = "img-circle",
        style = paste0("border: 1px solid red; opacity: ", input$opacity, ";")
      )
    }, deleteFile = TRUE)
  }
)
```

